<section class="landing-section landing-section--alt">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>You shouldn't need a design suite for one icon</h2>
    <p>When you just need an app icon or a simple logo, the same things get in the way.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Professional design tools have so many features that the first screen is already overwhelming.</li>
      <li>Free icon packs are easy to find, but changing their colors and background still means opening an editor.</li>
      <li>App icons come in many sizes, and resizing each one by hand is tedious.</li>
      <li>You can't tell which color combination works, so you tweak the same design over and over.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Icon Maker cuts this down to <strong>three layers</strong>. Pick an icon, fill it, and export every size you need in one go. Stuck on colors? <strong>Style ideas</strong> generates variations for you.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>Front icon + back icon + background</h2>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/01_overview.png" alt="Icon Maker editor — layer picker on the left, editing tools on the right" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>On the left of the editor, choose the <strong>Front · Back · Background</strong> layer; the tools on the right style only that layer. Each layer keeps its own style, so you can mix a gradient background with a solid icon and a drop shadow.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Preview</strong> in the top-left shows how it looks at real icon size</li>
      <li><strong>Swap</strong> exchanges the front and back layers</li>
      <li>The bottom bar has <strong>New · Open · Save · Export</strong> — save a design and keep editing it later</li>
      <li>First launch starts with a sample icon and a quick guide</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section landing-section--alt">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>Thousands of icons, letters, even your photos</h2>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/02_icons.png" alt="Select Icon — Material, System, Awesome, MDI, Symbols and Photo tabs with search by name" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>Layer content is organized in tabs, and you can search icons by name.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Material Icons · Font Awesome · MDI · Material Symbols</strong> — thousands of open-source icon glyphs</li>
      <li><strong>System</strong> — type letters or initials in your device fonts for a logo look</li>
      <li><strong>Photo</strong> — fill with a photo from your gallery or a sample photo. Double-tap to adjust position and size, and switch between Fit and Fill</li>
      <li>Tap an empty layer to open the picker right away</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>Fill — solid, gradient or photo</h2>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/03_fill.png" alt="Gradient fill — preset palettes such as warm, cool, nature and sunset" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>Choose what goes inside each layer. Changes show up on the canvas instantly, so you pick while looking at the result.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Solid</strong> — color picker or recently used colors</li>
      <li><strong>Gradient</strong> — linear, radial and sweep. Start from preset palettes (warm, cool, nature, sunset…) or set start/end points and color stops yourself</li>
      <li><strong>Photo</strong> — fill the icon shape with a picture</li>
      <li><strong>Stroke</strong> — outline color and thickness</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section landing-section--alt">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>Shapes and transforms</h2>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/04_shape.png" alt="Shape settings — width, height, corner radius and rectangle, oval, triangle, star, diamond, hexagon, heart" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>Pick the base shape — <strong>rectangle, oval, triangle, star, diamond, hexagon or heart</strong> — and set width, height and corner radius with sliders. Common app-icon shapes like the Android squircle or the iOS rounded square are one radius away.</p>
    <p><strong>Transform</strong> moves, rotates, scales and skews a layer, and <strong>Perspective</strong> adds a tilted 3D look.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>Blur · Emboss · Shadow</h2>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/05_effect.png" alt="Emboss settings — light direction, intensity and height" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>Three effects that add depth to a flat icon.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Blur</strong> — soft, natural blur</li>
      <li><strong>Emboss</strong> — drag the light direction on a dial, then tune intensity and height for a raised look</li>
      <li><strong>Shadow</strong> — fine control over position, color and blur radius</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section landing-section--alt">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>Style ideas — variations of your design at a glance</h2>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/08_style_board.png" alt="Style ideas board — cards around your design and mood variations" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>Not sure which colors work best? Tap <strong>Style ideas</strong> in the editor and a board of variation cards built from your current design appears.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Around your design</strong> — cards that change <em>one thing at a time</em>, such as back hue, background hue or front rotation. The middle column is your current design</li>
      <li><strong>Moods</strong> — the whole design re-styled as Minimal, Gradient, Clay, Glass, Neon, Luxe or Pastel</li>
      <li>Add favorites to <strong>Picks</strong> and export several at once</li>
    </ul>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/09_style_card.png" alt="Style card detail — compare with original, home screen previews, Add to picks and Apply now" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>Tap a card to compare it side by side with the original and preview it <strong>on your home screen</strong> (Circle · Squircle · Rounded · Small). <strong>Apply now</strong> can be undone right away, and <strong>More like this</strong> explores closer variations around that card.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>Export every size you need in one go</h2>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/07_export.png" alt="Export — check multiple sizes from 64 to 1024 and save as PNG" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>Finished icons are saved as transparent <strong>PNG</strong> files. Check as many sizes as you need, <strong>from 64 × 64 up to 1024 × 1024</strong>, and they are all generated at once — 1024 for the store listing, 512 for the launcher, 64 for a favicon, without resizing each by hand.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landing-section landing-section--alt">
  <div class="landing-section__inner">
    <h2>Dark mode</h2>
    <img src="/assets/images/iconmixer/screenshots/en/06_dark.png" alt="Editor in dark mode" class="app-screenshot" loading="lazy">
    <p>Built on Material Design, the app follows your system dark mode setting — handy for checking how your icon colors read on a dark background.</p>
  </div>
</section>

